oaxaca-installer (0.1.11) stonking; urgency=medium

  * The installation copies only the medium's installed-system layer
    (casper/filesystem.squashfs), so the live session's packages never reach
    the disk, and the packages step that removed them ("Removing 5
    packages") is gone, with the network it needed for apt-get update
    (docs/7, choice 55).
  * snapshots-setup is now filesystem-setup (shellprocess@filesystem): it
    installs the root filesystem's tools from the medium's package pool,
    btrfs-progs and Timeshift on btrfs, xfsprogs on xfs, which the layer
    copied to the disk does not carry.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0500

oaxaca-installer (0.1.10) stonking; urgency=medium

  * The partition page starts on btrfs: availableFileSystemTypes lists btrfs
    first. Calamares fills the file system dropdowns from that list in order
    and starts on its first entry, whatever defaultFileSystemType says, so
    0.1.8 and 0.1.9 still offered ext4 first.

