oaxaca-installer (0.1.6) stonking; urgency=medium

  * snapshots-setup, run as shellprocess@snapshots before the packages
    step: on a btrfs root filesystem, mark btrfs-progs and Timeshift as
    installed by hand, so the packages step's apt-get autoremove keeps
    them, and write /etc/timeshift/timeshift.json for the root filesystem
    (docs/7 choice 51). Until now every install lost btrfs-progs to that
    autoremove, a btrfs install included.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

oaxaca-installer (0.1.5) stonking; urgency=medium

  * keep-previous-loader: on an EFI System Partition of the target's own
    (no /EFI/ubuntu/grub.cfg stub, as after "Erase disk"), keep nothing: it
    had still added a menu entry for every other system with its own /boot,
    which on a machine with one disk per system points at another disk and
    outlives it when that disk is wiped; each system boots from its own
    disk through the firmware's boot menu.

